# Props, bodies, and composition

**Prerequisites:** [pure components](/docs/concepts/pure-components/).
**Kind:** concept.
**Next:** [Author components](/docs/how-to/author-components/).

The first parameter is a props record. Nested markup is a second `Html`
argument, not a `children` field on that record. Putting `Html` in the record
wraps it in `Html.text` and escapes it.

Calls are Roc function calls after lowering. `<Design.Button />` is
`Design.button({ … })`. Missing PascalCase names fail in Roc, not in a
client-side registry lookup.

Self-closing tags pass only props. Paired tags pass the body. Fragments group
siblings without inventing a wrapper component.

**Related:** [Components](/docs/reference/language/components/).
